# Trivy — accepted findings for clinical-trial-patient-match:latest
###################################################################
#
# ONE LINE PER CVE. No package wildcards, no severity downgrade, no `--ignore-
# unfixed` substitute — the gate already skips unfixed findings on its own
# argument, and this file is only for findings that DO have a fix and still
# cannot be taken here.
#
# NOTHING IN THIS FILE IS FIXED. Every CVE below is present in the image that
# ships. The gate is green because these are accepted, not because they are
# absent, and the non-gating FULL scan step in the workflow prints all of them
# on every run so they stay visible.
#
# A new CVE against any package named here still fails the gate — that is the
# property a package-level ignore would destroy, and it is why this file is
# written out one id at a time.
#
# THREE BLOCKING CLASSES, mirroring .github/scripts/audit_gate.py so the two
# gates cannot drift in their reasoning:
#
#   (THE `SCOPE` CLASS IS GONE, AND SO ARE ITS ELEVEN ENTRIES.) It held
#            apache-airflow 3.1.7 -- two CRITICALs and nine HIGHs -- accepted on
#            the argument that upgrading "changes the scheduler, the metadata
#            database schema and the REST API". The upgrade to 3.3.0 is done and
#            verified, so the entries are deleted rather than left to rot. See
#            pyproject.toml's `orchestration` extra for the per-version
#            measurement that chose the target.
#
#   PIN-CAP  another pinned dependency's metadata forbids the fixed version.
#            pillow: every fix is 12.x; streamlit 1.46.0 says `pillow<12` and
#            fastembed 0.7.4 says `pillow<12.0`. The earliest streamlit lifting
#            that cap is 1.51.0, which changes 96 values in the committed
#            dashboard snapshot (43 True->False, four figure heights to 0).
#
#            THE starlette ENTRIES ARE GONE TOO, and they were not accepted
#            away -- they are fixed. `fastapi==0.117.1` declared
#            `starlette<0.49.0`, which is what made every starlette fix
#            unreachable. The Airflow upgrade forced fastapi to 0.136.3
#            (apache-airflow-core 3.3.0 requires `fastapi>=0.129.0,<0.137.0`),
#            starlette resolves to 1.6.0, and all three ids that were listed
#            here now report clean against the built image.
#
#   MODEL    transformers is the MedCPT cross-encoder's loader and Stage 3's
#            ranking is what the twelve characterization fixtures pin. Those
#            fixtures cannot currently be replayed to prove a bump safe — the
#            Qdrant alias moved to trial_criteria_20260807_111807 while they
#            are pinned to ...20260803_104642 — so the one mechanism built to
#            verify this change is unavailable.

